+### Supplied spectrum (`-hhl_spectrum`, work-plan item 19)
+
+The HHL path needs three spectral numbers: a scale for A, the condition
+number kappa of the encoded matrix (it sizes the clock register,
+`nl = max(nb + 1, ceil(log2(kappa + 1))) + 1`), and the bounds lambda_min,
+lambda_max of its |eigenvalues| (they set the reciprocal constant and the
+evolution time). By default (`-hhl_spectrum internal`) fvm scales A by its
+spectral radius (a full `np.linalg.eig`), and the HHL library computes
+kappa and the bounds itself (`NumPyMatrix.condition_bounds()`, a full SVD,
+and `eigs_bounds()`, a full eigendecomposition). A deflated run then pays
+for these on top of the pre-step SVD.
+
+`-hhl_spectrum deflation` (with `-hhl_deflate_k K >= 1`) takes all three
+from the pre-step instead. The library is called with
+`construct_circuit(..., condition_bound=, eigenvalue_bounds=)` (fork API,
+`linear_solvers.SpectralInfo` records what it used), so neither of its
+internal calls runs, and fvm scales A' by sigma_max, so no eig of A' runs.
+
+How the values follow from the SVD of the ORIGINAL A (0-based ascending,
+sigma_K the (K+1)-th smallest, sigma_max the largest):
+
+1. A' keeps sigma_K .. sigma_max of A and parks K values at sigma_max, so
+   sigma_min(A') = sigma_K and sigma_max(A') = sigma_max.
+2. Scaling by s divides every singular value by s. With s = sigma_max they
+   lie in [sigma_K / sigma_max, 1].
+3. Padding to the next power of 2 adds an identity block. Its singular
+   values are 1, inside that range, so they change no bound.
+4. Hermitian doubling H = [[0, P], [P^H, 0]] has eigenvalues +- the
+   singular values of P. So |eig(H)| are exactly those singular values.
+
+The encoded matrix therefore has lambda_min = sigma_K / sigma_max,
+lambda_max = 1 and kappa = sigma_max / sigma_K = `kappa_eff`. In general,
+for any scale s with sigma_min <= s <= sigma_max of the matrix handed to
+HHL, lambda_min = sigma_min / s, lambda_max = sigma_max / s, kappa =
+sigma_max / sigma_min; the default s = spectral radius always satisfies
+this, so the same identity describes the internal path. `hhl_spectrum.py`
+holds the derivation and `tests/test_hhl_spectrum.py` checks it to 1e-10
+against `np.linalg.cond` / `eigvals` of H on every archived Jacobian.
 
+The HHL circuit depends on A only through A / lambda_min and the ratio
+lambda_min / lambda_max, so the different scale gives the same quantum
+solve of the system block. Only the small absolute offsets fvm adds to b
+(1e-12 on every entry, 1e-8 on the padded entries) do not scale with s,
+which leaves round-off-level differences. Measured at nelem 2, K = 1 (archived iteration
+0): same clock register (6 qubits), and the solution differs from the
+default deflated path by 1.9e-12 max-abs and from the internal bounds of
+the same encoded matrix by 1.1e-14. The circuit itself differs (the
+padding block sits at another phase), so its qpy files are keyed
+`..._deflate<K>_specdeflation.qpy`. Supplying exactly the internal values
+gives the identical circuit (`quantum_tools.circuit_key`).
+
+Six HHL `qc_metadata` columns sit after `t_svd_s`:
+
+| column | type | meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `hhl_spectrum` | str | `internal` or `deflation`; empty only for a `-loadcirc` circuit saved before item 19 |
+| `hhl_a_scale` | float | the scale s: A_q / s before padding (the spectral radius, or sigma_max under `deflation`) |
+| `hhl_kappa` | float | kappa of the encoded Hermitian matrix that sized the clock register |
+| `hhl_lambda_min`, `hhl_lambda_max` | float | its |eigenvalue| bounds used for the circuit (lambda_min after the library's near-zero substitution) |
+| `t_spectrum_s` | float, s | wall time of this step's spectral work for the circuit: the spectral-radius eig plus the library's bound calls (that part is inside `circ_generate_time`); 0.0 under `deflation`, whose cost is `t_svd_s` |
+
+The pickle carries `hhl_spectrum` and `hhl_spectral_diag` next to
+`hhl_deflate_k`, and `quantum_circuit` carries the last step's
+`hhl_spectrum`, `hhl_a_scale`, `hhl_kappa`, `hhl_lambda_min`,
+`hhl_lambda_max`. The generated and transpiled qpy files keep the same
+record in their circuit metadata, so `-loadcirc` restores it.
+
+Diagnostics. `condition_number` and `lambda_*_orig` / `lambda_*_scaled` are
+metadata only (two full cond and two eigvals per step, outside every
+timing). `-hhl_spectral_diag off` skips them (empty cells; deflation only,
+since at K = 0 `kappa` is that condition number). The determinant and
+condition-number prints of `math_tools` run at `-v 1` and above only; with
+`-v 0 -hhl_spectrum deflation -hhl_spectral_diag off` the only dense
+spectral call left on the path is the pre-step SVD. At these sizes the
+saving is small (the library's two calls took 0.2 ms on the 32 x 32
+nelem-5 system, against 26 s of circuit construction); it matters for the
+item-18 cost comparison and at larger N.
